## Quickstart

Install [Pixi](https://pixi.sh/), then bootstrap the locked workspace, native and
WASM bindings, and git hooks:

```sh
pixi install -e full --locked
pixi run -e full tools run repo install
pixi run -e full tools run bindings build
pixi run -e full tools run repo hooks
```

Every repository and agent script runs through the single Pixi task
`pixi run [-e <env>] tools` (Python Tasknest `0.4.0`). Explore the task graph
with `pixi run tools ls`, or ask for one task's options with `pixi run tools help <task>`.

## Task reference

These tasks group by the question they answer. Run any of them with
`pixi run [-e <env>] tools run <task>`.

### Verify the repository

```sh
pixi run -e full tools run check      # Policy, schemas, docs, formatting, and linters
pixi run -e full tools run test       # Rust + Python + TypeScript tests & conformance
pixi run -e full tools run coverage   # Audit coverage/<lang>/ reports against the 90% threshold
pixi run -e full tools run compat     # Rust + Python + TypeScript/npm compatibility gates
```

### Per-ecosystem gates

```sh
pixi run -e full tools run rust compat      # Feature matrix, cargo package, isolated .crate test
pixi run -e full tools run python compat    # Maturin wheel/sdist, METADATA, offline venv smoke
pixi run -e full tools run ts compat        # Tarball pack, publint, attw, Bun, Node.js, and tsc
pixi run -e ffi tools run ffi build         # Compile polylib-ffi & generate Kotlin, Swift, Ruby
pixi run -e ffi tools run ffi test          # Run Kotlin (Gradle/Cucumber) & Ruby (Minitest/Cucumber)
pixi run -e ffi tools run ffi compat        # Verify Kotlin JAR (standalone JVM), Swift C-ABI/SwiftPM, Ruby gem
```

### Compatibility matrices

```sh
pixi run -e full tools run tox         # Unified tox runner (-m compat/python/npm/rust/ffi/all)
pixi run -e full tools run rust tox    # Tox Rust envs (features, packages, consumer, compat)
pixi run -e full tools run python tox  # Tox Python matrix (py310-py314, wheel/sdist)
pixi run -e full tools run ts tox      # Tox npm envs (pack, bun, node, types, compat)
pixi run -e ffi tools run ffi tox      # Tox UniFFI envs (kotlin-compat, ruby-compat, swift-compat)
```

## Quality and policy guardrails

- **Single automation entrypoint:** `pixi.toml` declares only
  `[tasks] tools = "python -B -m tasknest"`, root `package.json` has no
  `"scripts"`, and `lefthook.yml` delegates every hook through
  `pixi run [-e <env>] tools`.
- **Clean Code and boundaries:** `rude` + `rude-clean-code` (`CC0`–`CC9`,
  `CC704`, `CC804`), `ruff`, strict `mypy`, `cargo clippy -- -D warnings`,
  `cargo-deny`, `biome`, `rumdl`, `vale` (Microsoft, alex, and house prose
  styles), `lychee`, `gherlint`, `actionlint`, and `.alint.yml` enforce
  repository hygiene.
- **Per-language coverage:** each language writes `coverage/<lang>/` (`lcov.info`
  or `jacoco.xml`) and enforces a 90% line threshold locally and in CI.
  Workflows upload each language independently to GitHub Actions artifacts
  (`coverage-<lang>`) and Codecov (`.codecov.yml` flags `rust`, `python`, `ts`,
  `kotlin`, `ruby`, and `swift`).
- **Offline sandbox:** `pixi-sandbox.toml` packs Linux (`linux-64`) locked
  environments and vendored Cargo sources (`cargo_vendor = true`) via
  `scripts/restore.sh`. Optional `kt`, `rb`, and `ffi` environments stay outside
  the `developer` bundle to preserve transport budgets.

## Releases and documentation

- **Build:** `.github/workflows/build.yml` compiles and packs all six
  ecosystems, generates `report.json`, renders `report.md` with Jinja2
  (`templates/build-report.md.j2`), and uploads `SHA256SUMS.txt`.
- **Publish:** `.github/workflows/publish.yml` publishes via OIDC Trusted
  Publishing to crates.io, PyPI, npm, and RubyGems, plus Maven Central, GitHub
  Packages, and GitHub Releases in isolated environments.
- **Documentation site:** `docs` exports a static Fumadocs site with
  `pixi run -e docs tools run docs build`. `.github/workflows/pages.yml` always
  validates and builds the site, and deploys only when GitHub Pages uses GitHub
  Actions (`ENABLE_PAGES=false` opts out).
- **Templated docs and GitHub forms:** edit `templates/` and run
  `pixi run tools run docs write`. CI verifies template parity with `docs check`.

